  "evidence_limits": [
    "The video demonstrates successful logpoint creation, captured event rows and captured variables. It retains the actual visible success toasts and the original transition from the initial Enable logs banner to populated events after visiting Logs and reloading the session.",
    "Log Explorer displays 45 logs and recent nonzero histogram bars. The lack of an intervening enablement/settings change is established by the run chronology and contiguous navigation footage, not by the count alone.",
    "The first visible locals panel appears at source 1592.10s (09:31:17.100 UTC): quantity=3, discount_eligible=False, subtotal_cents=3600, discount_cents=0, total_cents=3600 and unit_price_cents=1200. This is the deliberately planted application bug, not a Datadog pricing or capture defect. The intended total 3240 is task context, not displayed UI text.",
    "The quantity-two comparison appears at source 1916.75s (09:36:41.750 UTC), with subtotal/total 2400 and discount 0. These source clocks identify observed UI frames; event-list timestamps may identify earlier events.",
    "The numeric-template update success toast appears at source 2448.70s (09:45:33.700 UTC). The later source 11 rows visibly render quantity 3 total 3600 and quantity 4 total 4320. The complete later 2/3/4 message-plus-locals control sequence belongs to separate source 12 evidence.",
    "The duration menu visibly offers 1 Hour, 1 Day, 2 Days and 1 Week. This is evidence for the displayed menu, not a universal API/product minimum.",
    "The repository-source warning remains visible during captured values. Successful runtime capture must not be equated with successful repository-source retrieval.",
    "The approved reset and a fresh selected-repository draft occur near the end. Recording stops at 09:53:41.25 UTC before Install & Authorize and OAuth completion at approximately 09:54\u201309:55; those later outcomes are screenshot-only and are not reconstructed here.",
    "The billing excerpt shows GitHub Free at $0.00/month and zero displayed usage; it does not show a numeric Actions-minute allowance. The SDK excerpt reports registration booleans; registration alone is not proof of captured values.",
    "All motion plays at original speed and includes original waiting time within every retained section. Titles, caption bands, cropping, one 2\u00d7nearest-neighbor enlargement of the uninstall dialog and opaque masks are disclosed editorial changes. No screenshot slideshow, generated image or reconstructed interaction is substituted.",
